#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078181 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078463 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "952a09bc-d1fa-5e2d-b146-ec28e1c960a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Nth Term of an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/id #uuid "3efc515d-87bd-5e90-b2ea-4bdf954302e5" :question/math-academy-id "e-14382" :question/problem "Find the formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence if the first term is $3$ and the common difference is $2.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\na_n= a_{1}+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the first term is $a_1={\\color{blue}3}$ and the common difference is $d={\\color{red}2}.$ So, we substitute into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\ta_n\t&= a_{1}+(n-1)d \\[3pt]\n\t\t\t&= {\\color{blue}3} + (n - 1)({\\color{red}2})  \\[3pt]\n\t\t\t&= 3 + 2n -2 \\[3pt]\n\t\t\t& =2n+1\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore the formula for the $n$th term is $a_n = 2n+1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078182 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078464 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f6a51df-54c6-5019-a5a0-05949d440895" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Nth Term of an Arithmetic Sequence in Function Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "fa9f6acf-041b-5030-a32a-065b562a7f49" :question/math-academy-id "e-14384" :question/problem "Find the formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence if the first term is $0$ and the second term is $-2.$ Express your answer in function notation." :question/worked-solution "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence (in function notation) is\n\n$$\nf(n)= f(1)+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nWe are given the first term $f(1)={\\color{blue}0}.$ Also, the common difference of the sequence can be found as\n\n$$\nd=-2 - 0 = {\\color{red}-2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we substitute into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\nf(n)&= f(1)+(n-1)d \\[3pt]\n&= {\\color{blue}0} + (n - 1)({\\color{red}-2})  \\[3pt]\n&= 0 - 2n + 2 \\[3pt]\n&= 2 - 2n\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is $f(n) = 2 - 2n.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078184 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078465 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8234e8b-2b1c-5433-94f8-64f84f38f1d0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Particular Term of an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/id #uuid "27c03d66-4cbe-567c-8846-4d6b0382bd89" :question/math-academy-id "e-14387" :question/problem "Find the $50$th term of the following arithmetic sequence.\n\n$$\n-5, \\: -8, \\: -11, \\: \\ldots\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\na_n= a_{1}+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nFirst, we will write the formula for the $n$th term of this sequence. From the first few terms\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}-5}, \\: -8, \\: -11, \\ldots,\n$$\n\nwe see that the first term is $a_1={\\color{blue}-5}$ and the common difference is \n\n$$\nd=-8-(-5)={\\color{red}-3}.\n$$\n\nSo, we substitute into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\na_n&= a_{1}+(n-1)d \\[3pt]\n&= {\\color{blue}-5} + (n - 1)({\\color{red}-3})  \\[3pt]\n& =-5 -3n + 3 \\[3pt]\n&=-3n-2\n}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use our formula to find the $50$th term. All we have to do is substitute $n=50\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\na_n &=-3n-2 \\[7pt]\na_{50} &= -3(50)-2 \\[3pt]\n&= -150-2 \\[3pt]\n&= -152\t\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $50$th term of the sequence is $a_{50}=-152.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078186 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078466 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85635ba4-d618-5600-8531-eacb2b0bb5d0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Nth Term Given Another Term and the Common Difference"}] :question/id #uuid "56926a19-7cfc-51ca-8f07-870fc0271abb" :question/math-academy-id "e-14391" :question/problem "Find the formula for the $n$th term of the arithmetic sequence that has a $7$th term equal to $-34$ and a common difference of $-5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $a_{7}=-34$ is $6$ jumps after $a_1$.\n\n![](images/ea/ea803977d4861ad654bd29ff15f706fdd1d11f71dbf7c885f175fe8168f21b66.png)\n\nHence, we can write\n\n$$\na_{7} = a_1 + 6d,\n$$\n\nand solve for $a_1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{7} & ={a}_{1}+6d \\\\ -34 & ={a}_{1}+6(-5) \\\\ -34 & ={a}_{1}-30 \\\\ -4 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-4+(n-1)(-5) \\\\  & =-4-5n+5 \\\\  & =1-5n.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078778 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078463 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "952a09bc-d1fa-5e2d-b146-ec28e1c960a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Nth Term of an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c1d05ff-438c-5f82-b8ed-53c691355ff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6n-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c1d05ff-438c-5f82-b8ed-53c691355ff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6n-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519086} :answer-field/id #uuid "88ea8e4e-ad84-59d2-88ae-fad1a6eafa0b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075709}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b044a7b4-bf4e-530c-bcd5-d3b3155a4c30" :question/math-academy-id "q-214167" :question/problem "Find the formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence if the first term is $3$ and the second term is $9.$\n\n${a}_{n}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,n\\ge 1$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nWe are given the first term ${a}_{1}=3.$ Also, the common difference of the sequence can be found as\n\n$$\nd=9-3=6.\n$$\n\nSo, we substitute into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =3+(n-1)(6) \\\\  & =3+6n-6 \\\\  & =6n-3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519581 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078465 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8234e8b-2b1c-5433-94f8-64f84f38f1d0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Particular Term of an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b362f619-d001-5550-b24b-0b7f5e3c596c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b362f619-d001-5550-b24b-0b7f5e3c596c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519287} :answer-field/id #uuid "10dee7ea-51b0-5e81-8645-f21eaee40664" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c129ef1c-2ac1-51e8-b05a-e3f368cf0b6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-214183" :question/problem "Consider the following arithmetic sequence.\n\n$$\n7,\\,3,\\,-1,\\,-5,\\,…\n$$\n\nWhat is the $34$th term of this sequence?\n\n${a}_{34}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nFirst, we will write the formula for the $n$th term of this sequence. From the first few terms\n\n$$\n7,\\,3,\\,-1,\\,-5,\\,…,\n$$\n\nwe see that the first term is ${a}_{1}=7$ and the common difference is \n\n$$\nd=3-7=-4.\n$$\n\nSo, we substitute into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =7+(n-1)(-4) \\\\  & =7-4n+4 \\\\  & =11-4n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use our formula to find the $34$th term. All we have to do is substitute $n=34:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =11-4n \\\\ {a}_{34} & =11-4(34) \\\\  & =11-136 \\\\  & =-125\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519512 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078465 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8234e8b-2b1c-5433-94f8-64f84f38f1d0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Particular Term of an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a218f878-fb16-539b-b22d-b8217b3611ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "127" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a218f878-fb16-539b-b22d-b8217b3611ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "127" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519257} :answer-field/id #uuid "e60cf3ae-4bd3-5233-9ad0-0f3680423eff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "013f16dc-6316-5e58-8d55-c6702c89f1f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-236631" :question/problem "Consider the following arithmetic sequence.\n\n$$\n-13,\\,-9,\\,-5,\\,-1,\\,…\n$$\n\nWhat is the $36$th term of this sequence?\n\n${a}_{36}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nFirst, we will write the formula for the $n$th term of this sequence. From the first few terms\n\n$$\n-13,\\,-9,\\,-5,\\,-1,\\,…,\n$$\n\nwe see that the first term is ${a}_{1}=-13$ and the common difference is \n\n$$\nd=-9-(-13)=4.\n$$\n\nSo, we substitute into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-13+(n-1)(4) \\\\  & =-13+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n-17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use our formula to find the $36$th term. All we have to do is substitute $n=36:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =4n-17 \\\\ {a}_{36} & =4(36)-17 \\\\  & =144-17 \\\\  & =127\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519534 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078466 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85635ba4-d618-5600-8531-eacb2b0bb5d0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Nth Term Given Another Term and the Common Difference"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c7c8818-c782-5316-80da-ffd05ab11d65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4n-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c7c8818-c782-5316-80da-ffd05ab11d65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4n-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519012} :answer-field/id #uuid "66a0ebd0-c132-5683-85ec-156c80eb20e0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519448}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36a772ef-4e2c-580e-97bd-8718ab74d591" :question/math-academy-id "q-236649" :question/problem "Find the formula for the $n$th term of the arithmetic sequence that has ${a}_{25}=95$ and the common difference $d=4.$\n\n${a}_{n}=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,n\\ge 1$" :question/worked-solution "Since ${a}_{25}=95$ is $24$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we can determine the first term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{25} & ={a}_{1}+24d \\\\ 95 & ={a}_{1}+24(4) \\\\ 95 & ={a}_{1}+96 \\\\ -1 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-1+(n-1)(4) \\\\  & =-1+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n-5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519562 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078464 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f6a51df-54c6-5019-a5a0-05949d440895" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Nth Term of an Arithmetic Sequence in Function Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30f18ff3-8803-5b11-b715-566a43baad55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=8-8n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519069} {:answer/id #uuid "3d98fcee-0127-556a-9c59-b169c73657ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=12-4n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519090} {:answer/id #uuid "589da9c7-c786-52ba-ac87-f1033636dc73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=8+4n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519124} {:answer/id #uuid "a723d771-0731-523c-87d1-fa2865987176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519267} {:answer/id #uuid "e28d317f-755b-5cbc-bd91-2aa99f3df59b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=4-4n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d98fcee-0127-556a-9c59-b169c73657ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=12-4n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519090} :answer-field/id #uuid "19425ac1-ab9b-59bf-ab5e-e629e3ebf1e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8eb6a381-be92-55fb-a425-16a442e609ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-5284" :question/problem "Find the general formula  for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence that begins with \n\n$$\n8,\\,4,\\,0,\\,…\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence (in function notation) is\n\n$$\nf(n)=f(1)+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nFrom the first few terms\n\n$$\n8,\\,4,\\,0,\\,…,\n$$\n\nwe see that the first term is $f(1)=8$ and the common difference is \n\n$$\nd=4-8=-4.\n$$\n\nSo, we substitute into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)+(n-1)d \\\\  & =8+(n-1)(-4) \\\\  & =8-4n+4 \\\\  & =12-4n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is $f(n)=12-4n.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519566 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078463 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "952a09bc-d1fa-5e2d-b146-ec28e1c960a9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Nth Term of an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "050708e2-6739-52e9-a46f-7cb0ac68aaf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=5n-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518995} {:answer/id #uuid "5dfa4269-cbb8-59e7-a7f8-f135398c2025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=n-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519132} {:answer/id #uuid "7e21d868-17ef-5b93-99b4-bc4569ef160b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=4+n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519190} {:answer/id #uuid "aebb7654-fbed-542c-a4bc-79c62b80278b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=5n-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519275} {:answer/id #uuid "ce2dabb7-fe80-557d-a625-d071ad95e3f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-5n-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e21d868-17ef-5b93-99b4-bc4569ef160b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=4+n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519190} :answer-field/id #uuid "05d3aa33-1231-5643-97cb-aa9155290797" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519415}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b2690e5-910c-5f9f-9900-ab879a8e0507" :question/math-academy-id "q-5288" :question/problem "Find the formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence if the first term is $5$ and the common difference is $1.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the first term is ${a}_{1}=5$ and the common difference is $d=1.$ So, we substitute into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =5+(n-1)(1) \\\\  & =5+n-1 \\\\  & =4+n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the formula for the $n$th term is ${a}_{n}=4+n.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519600 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078464 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f6a51df-54c6-5019-a5a0-05949d440895" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Nth Term of an Arithmetic Sequence in Function Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b4fb817-c6ac-5573-bf1c-5cb3e3b8e337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=-2+6n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519034} {:answer/id #uuid "2fa48722-fce0-58fe-b017-004d5dd19c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=10-2n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519067} {:answer/id #uuid "788facef-43a8-5a7d-a331-a2690d5bf0e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=10-6n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519180} {:answer/id #uuid "a8bcb7f8-b4e0-5766-86bd-8d08ad9105fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=2-6n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519270} {:answer/id #uuid "b080650d-ed5c-56d2-bdb9-2577c9308fa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=6-2n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "788facef-43a8-5a7d-a331-a2690d5bf0e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(n)=10-6n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519180} :answer-field/id #uuid "910c3056-976b-5fa4-a81b-5a9f980f88e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519465}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f4a1a68f-984f-511a-88be-72b335a1e5eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-76514" :question/problem "Find the formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence if the first term is $4$ and the second term is $-2.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence (in function notation) is\n\n$$\nf(n)=f(1)+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nWe are given the first term $f(1)=4.$ Also, the common difference of the sequence can be found as\n\n$$\nd=-2-4=-6.\n$$\n\nSo, we substitute into the formula and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)+(n-1)d \\\\  & =4+(n-1)(-6) \\\\  & =4-6n+6 \\\\  & =10-6n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is $f(n)=10-6n.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519543 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078466 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85635ba4-d618-5600-8531-eacb2b0bb5d0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Formula for the Nth Term Given Another Term and the Common Difference"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "806f0976-cc03-5853-8177-97913af01160" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-4n+40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519194} {:answer/id #uuid "b96bdae9-d9de-5734-a615-2c84228625cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-4n+36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519295} {:answer/id #uuid "bc3ef00d-b613-5fc9-bf0e-97d50b59965c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=4n-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519301} {:answer/id #uuid "d345e9f4-3bf0-5d26-852b-c84101a6e872" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=4n-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519339} {:answer/id #uuid "f65ad03b-76c0-5d45-8fb0-eb2a1ab3bb6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=4n-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc3ef00d-b613-5fc9-bf0e-97d50b59965c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{n}=4n-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519301} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ec14b21-c438-5bac-886f-56773de8e73f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59d1d85b-3b0d-5f71-98d3-9151bc5e371c" :question/math-academy-id "q-76518" :question/problem "Given an arithmetic sequence that has ${a}_{8}=8$ and the common difference $d=4$, what is the general formula for the $n$th term of the sequence?" :question/worked-solution "Since ${a}_{8}=8$ is $7$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we can determine the first term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{8} & ={a}_{1}+7d \\\\ 8 & ={a}_{1}+7(4) \\\\ 8 & ={a}_{1}+28 \\\\ -20 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-20+(n-1)(4) \\\\  & =-20+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n-24\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
